   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project for Agri-food and Agro-industry Development Assistance in Pakistan: Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the competitiveness, safety, inclusiveness and resilience of the meat and dairy industries in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa. It will scale up the meat-sector interventions introduced under PAFAID Phase I, including improved food safety and hygiene practices, risk-based inspection, training through AHITI, support to butcher shops and meat processors, and expansion of the Safe Meat Competition across the province. In parallel, the project will introduce new dairy value chain interventions in Mansehra, Peshawar, Dera Ismail Khan, and Mardan, focusing on milk safety and testing, improved handling and cold-chain practices, model milk retail and packaging solutions, dairy processing, and value addition in products such as yogurt, cheese and butter.  The project will strengthen regulatory and laboratory functions, expand sustainable technical support services through AHITI and partner institutions, and upgrade meat businesses in districts beyond the original Phase I pilots. Further the project will support dairy associations, cooperatives and small agribusinesses with hygienic milk handling, chilling, processing, product development, packaging and market access.</narrative>
  </description>
